From c340bb75fd71b0970c306e6ece1fe6812482f88f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NayiemW <37852059+NayiemW@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 04:56:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Give a rebuilt state the live node's round-start ranks

The live node's behaviour is canonical: a delegate's rank is set at
round starts only and holds for the whole round. A running node calls
DposState.buildDelegateRanking in RoundState.applyRound at each round
start and nowhere else, so a delegate ranked at the start of round R
keeps that rank until the start of R+1 (even if it resigns), and a
delegate not ranked then (resigned at that moment, or registered later)
has no rank until the start of R+1 (even if it revokes).

A state rebuilt at start did not follow this. The StateBuilder's last
step, buildDelegateRanking, ranks every non-resigned delegate on the
current state. RoundState.restore() then calls
calcPreviousActiveDelegates, which copies the round-start rank back
only to the delegates that were ranked at the round start; every other
delegate kept its fresh rank. Example: genesis_53 resigned at 69 and
revoked at 176, and after a restart at 190 without a saved state it had
rank 53 next to tx1n2290, which holds rank 53 on the live node. A
delegate registered inside the round got a rank too. Solar 4.3.1
unmodified does the same.

calcPreviousActiveDelegates now also removes delegate.rank from every
delegate that was not ranked at the round start. The same function
serves a revert across a round boundary (revertRound), which had the
same flaw and now also returns exactly the ranks of the round it goes
back into. Delegates ranked at the round start, the round's forging
list and the rewards are unchanged; the saved-state path already
matched and still does.

Block validity, the forging list and the rewards use the round-start
ranks, which do not change. What changes are the ranks the API shows
and the node-local count of ranked delegates (Peer.activeDelegates),
which now match the live node after a restart.

Test: patches/tests/47-restart-rank-consistency.test.js. The example
above, with the real Wallet, DposState and RoundState classes and
stub repositories (53 genesis delegates and tx1n2290; genesis_53
resigns at 69 and revokes at 176, genesis_10 resigns at 170, newcomer
registers at 180; restart at 190). The StateBuilder path now gives the
live ranks with no rank used twice (base: genesis_53 53 next to
tx1n2290 53, newcomer 1 next to genesis_1); a revert of 212 back into
round 4 gives round 4's ranks (base: the round 5 ranks stay). The
saved-state path, genesis_10's kept rank and the next round start are
unchanged.

The same restart on a running devnet (with patches 45 to 49): at 190 the
live state, the saved-state restart and the StateBuilder restart are
identical, genesis_53 has no rank and tx1n2290 alone has rank 53. The
chain then verified from height 2 to 265 with no problem, every block
at its scheduled slot.

Patch: 47
Consensus: no
